WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.380 --> 00:00:04.600
- [Mark] All right, J.J.

00:00:04.600 --> 00:00:05.433
- Yeah.

00:00:05.433 --> 00:00:06.266
- [Mark] J.J., where'd you grow up?

00:00:06.266 --> 00:00:07.099
Where are you from originally?

00:00:07.099 --> 00:00:10.100
- [J.J.] I grew up in
Los Angeles, California.

00:00:10.100 --> 00:00:10.933
- [Mark] And tell me about your family,

00:00:10.933 --> 00:00:12.800
you had both your parents
when you were a kid?

00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:15.310
- [J.J.] Well no, my family was divorced,

00:00:15.310 --> 00:00:18.103
divorced by the time I was five-years-old.

00:00:19.860 --> 00:00:21.450
- [Mark] You were raised by your mom?

00:00:21.450 --> 00:00:24.833
- Well, I was raised by my
father and my grandmother.

00:00:28.210 --> 00:00:29.440
- [Mark] And where was mom?

00:00:29.440 --> 00:00:31.840
- Well, my mother stayed
in Compton, California,

00:00:32.860 --> 00:00:37.860
and they kinda like took me
from her when I was of age,

00:00:38.030 --> 00:00:40.370
of born, like maybe two-years-old.

00:00:40.370 --> 00:00:42.583
My grandmother took me from my mother,

00:00:43.940 --> 00:00:47.950
because she felt I was my
father's kid after a while.

00:00:47.950 --> 00:00:50.750
So they took me, and then my
father and mother divorced.

00:00:51.690 --> 00:00:53.710
- [Mark] How would you
describe your childhood?

00:00:53.710 --> 00:00:58.450
- Well, I didn't really
understand my childhood.

00:00:58.450 --> 00:01:00.250
I didn't get to play a lot as a kid.

00:01:01.300 --> 00:01:02.500
My father kept me with him,

00:01:02.500 --> 00:01:05.390
always riding around in the car with him.

00:01:05.390 --> 00:01:09.313
And I just didn't have a lot
of friends at an early age,

00:01:12.380 --> 00:01:14.590
and from there

00:01:16.630 --> 00:01:20.593
my sister was my grandmother's favorite.

00:01:21.520 --> 00:01:25.680
And so what happened there
is after a while, my mother,

00:01:25.680 --> 00:01:29.050
when I turned about eight,
my mother wanted us back.

00:01:29.050 --> 00:01:32.670
So she went to court, and she got us back.

00:01:32.670 --> 00:01:34.830
And my grandmother just developed

00:01:34.830 --> 00:01:37.870
some real messed up feelings towards me,

00:01:37.870 --> 00:01:39.680
because she felt it was my fault

00:01:41.660 --> 00:01:43.377
for asking her, constantly asking her,

00:01:43.377 --> 00:01:45.700
"Where was my mother at?"

00:01:45.700 --> 00:01:49.860
And so my mother got us back.

00:01:49.860 --> 00:01:52.173
And from there,

00:01:53.210 --> 00:01:55.220
my mother started having problems

00:01:55.220 --> 00:01:57.090
with alcohol and drinking.

00:01:57.090 --> 00:02:00.330
So my father found another
reason to get us back.

00:02:00.330 --> 00:02:02.400
And once he got us back,

00:02:02.400 --> 00:02:05.543
my grandmother just had
this type of hatred for me.

00:02:06.600 --> 00:02:11.080
And she would just at a
early age, make me sweep,

00:02:11.080 --> 00:02:11.940
clean the house.

00:02:11.940 --> 00:02:13.890
She gave my sister everything,

00:02:13.890 --> 00:02:18.820
and didn't give me too
much of anything as a kid.

00:02:18.820 --> 00:02:22.160
And from there, my
grandfather used to take me

00:02:22.160 --> 00:02:22.993
in the back house.

00:02:22.993 --> 00:02:25.880
We had a back house also
with the front house, and

00:02:27.270 --> 00:02:30.410
my grandfather used to molest me as a kid,

00:02:30.410 --> 00:02:34.210
and make me

00:02:34.210 --> 00:02:36.710
just have oral sex with him as a kid,

00:02:36.710 --> 00:02:38.970
which I knew nothing about at that time.

00:02:38.970 --> 00:02:39.803
- [Mark] How old were you?

00:02:39.803 --> 00:02:44.803
- I was about seven and eight
when he used to do this.

00:02:45.040 --> 00:02:49.130
And I think once my
auntie came to the door,

00:02:49.130 --> 00:02:52.800
and she saw it, and she didn't
even say anything about it.

00:02:52.800 --> 00:02:55.350
She just kept doing what she was doing.

00:02:55.350 --> 00:02:58.390
So this kinda messed my
head up, coming up as a kid.

00:02:58.390 --> 00:03:02.750
I kinda thought that maybe
this was a part of life.

00:03:02.750 --> 00:03:05.600
I didn't know any better than that.

00:03:05.600 --> 00:03:09.010
And so, as I grew up and got older,

00:03:09.010 --> 00:03:13.120
I just didn't know
which way to go in life.

00:03:13.120 --> 00:03:16.763
And I ended up at a very
early age here on Skid Row,

00:03:17.630 --> 00:03:22.560
and I was here for wow, maybe 23,

00:03:22.560 --> 00:03:24.393
to age of 23 to now,

00:03:25.260 --> 00:03:29.420
being very indecisive on what life was.

00:03:29.420 --> 00:03:31.113
I always felt like I was alone,

00:03:33.307 --> 00:03:34.490
and nobody really cared.

00:03:34.490 --> 00:03:35.370
My family didn't.

00:03:35.370 --> 00:03:37.670
I remember once when I
went to stay with my mother

00:03:37.670 --> 00:03:42.210
at probably about 18 or 19,

00:03:42.210 --> 00:03:44.083
and try to give it another go.

00:03:45.650 --> 00:03:49.300
My stepfather at that
time, she was remarried.

00:03:49.300 --> 00:03:53.820
He didn't too much like me,

00:03:53.820 --> 00:03:57.170
so I ended up after going to work,

00:03:57.170 --> 00:03:59.950
I used to have to sleep in the cupboard

00:03:59.950 --> 00:04:03.870
in the car shed, in the
garage, in the parking stall.

00:04:03.870 --> 00:04:04.730
We had some apartments,

00:04:04.730 --> 00:04:07.790
and there was a parking stall
over the top of the garage.

00:04:07.790 --> 00:04:11.290
And I used to have to go
sleep inside the garage,

00:04:11.290 --> 00:04:13.550
the parking stall.

00:04:13.550 --> 00:04:16.190
And it's like, I can hear
my mother going to work

00:04:16.190 --> 00:04:17.640
in the morning, and start her car up.

00:04:17.640 --> 00:04:18.473
And she wouldn't even know

00:04:18.473 --> 00:04:20.200
that I'm literally in the parking stall,

00:04:20.200 --> 00:04:23.640
right above the car, going to sleep.

00:04:23.640 --> 00:04:27.740
And just had a horrible life growing up,

00:04:27.740 --> 00:04:30.250
having to go through all this stuff.

00:04:30.250 --> 00:04:32.470
I felt like nobody really cared,

00:04:32.470 --> 00:04:35.360
and I didn't know which way to go in life.

00:04:35.360 --> 00:04:37.340
And once I hit skid row,

00:04:37.340 --> 00:04:41.660
it was just so much of the
same type of stuff down here.

00:04:41.660 --> 00:04:43.150
A lot of people that was damaged,

00:04:43.150 --> 00:04:47.060
a lot of people that had mental
problems, or drug problems.

00:04:47.060 --> 00:04:48.840
And it's kinda like I felt

00:04:48.840 --> 00:04:52.690
that I was amongst people

00:04:52.690 --> 00:04:56.890
like myself, and I had
the same type of problems

00:04:56.890 --> 00:04:57.900
these people did.

00:04:57.900 --> 00:05:02.420
And it just turned into
pretty much all of my life.

00:05:02.420 --> 00:05:07.000
You know, being my age now,
I've been down here 38 years,

00:05:07.000 --> 00:05:11.160
and I never just had too much to go on.

00:05:11.160 --> 00:05:14.940
Never really nobody to
guide me, nobody to tell me

00:05:14.940 --> 00:05:17.670
that it was gonna be okay,
that it wasn't my fault,

00:05:17.670 --> 00:05:20.010
the things that happened to me as a kid.

00:05:20.010 --> 00:05:24.903
I was constantly beaten by
my grandmother, and my uncle,

00:05:25.780 --> 00:05:27.690
coming up for no reason at all.

00:05:27.690 --> 00:05:29.810
You know, something wasn't did right,

00:05:29.810 --> 00:05:32.710
or I said the wrong thing.

00:05:32.710 --> 00:05:35.230
So I constantly was always
getting beat and whooped

00:05:35.230 --> 00:05:39.220
by the family, and my life's just been

00:05:39.220 --> 00:05:41.580
a horror story, if you ask me.

00:05:41.580 --> 00:05:43.307
Just growing up, stuff,
I don't think a kid

00:05:43.307 --> 00:05:45.540
should have to go through,

00:05:45.540 --> 00:05:48.720
and I constantly a battle
with this, to the date.

00:05:48.720 --> 00:05:52.240
I constantly have to try to figure out,

00:05:52.240 --> 00:05:53.073
am I worth it?

00:05:53.073 --> 00:05:56.690
Or why did I have to go through
this type of stuff as a kid?

00:05:56.690 --> 00:06:01.150
And my life is a little better now,

00:06:01.150 --> 00:06:02.130
because I'm older,

00:06:02.130 --> 00:06:05.140
and I'm able to put a
lot of stuff behind me,

00:06:05.140 --> 00:06:09.120
and I try harder.

00:06:09.120 --> 00:06:11.683
But things just keep coming
into play that have to do

00:06:11.683 --> 00:06:16.683
with my childhood and all that.

00:06:16.940 --> 00:06:17.773
- [Mark] Intellectually,
you can understand

00:06:17.773 --> 00:06:19.970
that this is not your fault.

00:06:19.970 --> 00:06:20.810
- Yes.

00:06:20.810 --> 00:06:22.887
- [Mark] But that doesn't really help you,

00:06:22.887 --> 00:06:25.830
'cause your subconscious, your behavior.

00:06:25.830 --> 00:06:28.900
- No, it doesn't help me because
it's all I knew growing up.

00:06:28.900 --> 00:06:30.750
You gotta figure as a kid, when it starts

00:06:30.750 --> 00:06:34.620
at such an early age
and you're being beat,

00:06:34.620 --> 00:06:37.210
you're being molested, you're
going through all this stuff,

00:06:37.210 --> 00:06:39.863
and nobody says anything about it.

00:06:40.730 --> 00:06:42.760
You kinda start believing it's your fault.

00:06:42.760 --> 00:06:44.530
- [Mark] Did you ever feel
like anyone loved you?

00:06:44.530 --> 00:06:47.320
- No, I didn't feel like
I was loved as a kid.

00:06:47.320 --> 00:06:49.890
I felt like I was told
what to do all my life,

00:06:49.890 --> 00:06:52.350
and how to do it, and if
it wasn't did that way,

00:06:52.350 --> 00:06:55.100
then I was gonna be in
trouble for some reason.

00:06:55.100 --> 00:06:56.650
That's how it usually ended up.

00:06:59.350 --> 00:07:01.240
When I grew up and learned

00:07:01.240 --> 00:07:04.100
that what my grandfather
was doing, wasn't right.

00:07:04.100 --> 00:07:07.440
That even had more of a play on my mind,

00:07:07.440 --> 00:07:11.180
because now I had bottled
all this stuff inside of me,

00:07:11.180 --> 00:07:13.363
and I was afraid to let anyone know.

00:07:15.660 --> 00:07:18.750
My mother passed, not even knowing this.

00:07:18.750 --> 00:07:21.300
I never told her at all

00:07:21.300 --> 00:07:23.583
that I was constantly molested as a kid.

00:07:25.530 --> 00:07:26.893
She never even knew it,

00:07:28.400 --> 00:07:30.850
and she passed going to
her grave not even knowing

00:07:30.850 --> 00:07:33.840
what my grandfather on my father's side

00:07:33.840 --> 00:07:35.060
had constantly done to me.

00:07:35.060 --> 00:07:37.410
I just felt so ashamed of it,

00:07:37.410 --> 00:07:41.090
or I didn't know how to explain it to her.

00:07:41.090 --> 00:07:44.960
So I just kept that a
secret all of my life.

00:07:44.960 --> 00:07:47.730
This is probably only
the second or third time

00:07:47.730 --> 00:07:51.860
in my life that I've even
mentioned that to anybody.

00:07:51.860 --> 00:07:54.140
What had happened to me as a kid

00:07:54.140 --> 00:07:58.329
is just something I kept
as a secret inside of me.

00:07:58.329 --> 00:08:01.163
- [Mark] How has that affected
your life as an adult?

00:08:02.940 --> 00:08:05.370
- It's affected me a great deal.

00:08:05.370 --> 00:08:07.800
- [Mark] I'm certain it has,
but I'm wondering like--

00:08:07.800 --> 00:08:10.430
- Well, I feel unworthy.

00:08:10.430 --> 00:08:13.243
I feel unworthy of anything.

00:08:14.160 --> 00:08:18.140
I feel that mentally people can look at me

00:08:18.140 --> 00:08:21.143
and know that I have been through stuff.

00:08:22.260 --> 00:08:24.530
I'm hurt, I'm ashamed,

00:08:24.530 --> 00:08:28.658
and there was never nobody
to talk to about it.

00:08:28.658 --> 00:08:32.690
- [Mark] Have you had
romantic relationships?

00:08:32.690 --> 00:08:35.380
- Yes, I have had romantic relationships.

00:08:35.380 --> 00:08:37.270
- [Mark] With women or men?

00:08:37.270 --> 00:08:38.453
- With women mostly.

00:08:39.670 --> 00:08:41.450
Other things with men I would try,

00:08:41.450 --> 00:08:44.280
because I didn't know if this was me.

00:08:44.280 --> 00:08:45.850
- [Mark] Right, you get confused by the.

00:08:45.850 --> 00:08:47.530
- Yeah, I was confused.

00:08:47.530 --> 00:08:50.010
So I didn't know what
was going on in my life,

00:08:50.010 --> 00:08:54.743
so I just felt the right
way was with women.

00:08:55.870 --> 00:09:00.870
But I just didn't know what
I was gonna do in my life.

00:09:01.530 --> 00:09:05.263
So I've always been confused
sexually in that part,

00:09:06.340 --> 00:09:10.910
because of my lifestyle,
and I grew up like that,

00:09:10.910 --> 00:09:15.140
and I grew up not being
understood by women,

00:09:15.140 --> 00:09:17.840
because they never knew my background,

00:09:17.840 --> 00:09:20.140
and they never knew
what was wrong with me,

00:09:20.140 --> 00:09:22.040
why I would go through certain things.

00:09:24.000 --> 00:09:27.633
So my life has just been
a complete disaster,

00:09:29.680 --> 00:09:31.230
is the best I can put it.

00:09:31.230 --> 00:09:33.800
You know, it's just been
a disaster from day one,

00:09:33.800 --> 00:09:36.160
and to the point that some times I wonder

00:09:36.160 --> 00:09:38.280
if I was cursed or something.

00:09:38.280 --> 00:09:39.843
Maybe there's a curse over me,

00:09:41.220 --> 00:09:42.710
or my whole family or something.

00:09:42.710 --> 00:09:44.660
And I just didn't know,

00:09:44.660 --> 00:09:46.430
and there's nothing I can do about it.

00:09:46.430 --> 00:09:48.070
And that's the bad part about it,

00:09:48.070 --> 00:09:49.940
feeling that you going
through all this in life,

00:09:49.940 --> 00:09:52.470
and not feeling there's
nothing you can do about it.

00:09:52.470 --> 00:09:53.850
You know, there's no heeling to it,

00:09:53.850 --> 00:09:56.340
because it's just the way life is.

00:09:56.340 --> 00:09:58.500
- [Mark] Are you living on the street?

00:09:58.500 --> 00:10:00.260
- Yes, I'm on the streets now.

00:10:00.260 --> 00:10:01.760
I've been on the streets.

00:10:01.760 --> 00:10:04.220
Every now and then I'll
try to make a break,

00:10:04.220 --> 00:10:06.110
and do something positive,

00:10:06.110 --> 00:10:08.740
but I think because of
what I go through mentally,

00:10:08.740 --> 00:10:10.970
I always run back to this,

00:10:10.970 --> 00:10:13.520
because I don't know how
to really deal with people

00:10:15.200 --> 00:10:16.690
and what's expected of me.

00:10:16.690 --> 00:10:20.320
So I just come back to the streets,

00:10:20.320 --> 00:10:21.670
where I feel a part of it.

00:10:21.670 --> 00:10:23.420
- [Mark] Yeah, are
drugs part of your life?

00:10:23.420 --> 00:10:25.600
- [J.J.] Drugs is part of my life also.

00:10:25.600 --> 00:10:29.993
I think I started using
drugs to self-medicate,

00:10:30.940 --> 00:10:35.940
and to try to block the
memories of what I go through.

00:10:36.720 --> 00:10:40.020
And a lot of times they
would help, not knowing

00:10:40.020 --> 00:10:41.760
that what they were doing
was actually putting me

00:10:41.760 --> 00:10:44.060
in more to the whole lifestyle,

00:10:44.060 --> 00:10:48.490
and becoming an addict
because of the drug scene.

00:10:48.490 --> 00:10:52.240
And I think that entrapped
me even more into Skid Row,

00:10:52.240 --> 00:10:57.040
not being aware, or
practicing right and wrong,

00:10:57.040 --> 00:10:58.503
or what's good and bad.

00:10:59.460 --> 00:11:02.263
This whole thing down here
has became a lifestyle to me.

00:11:06.839 --> 00:11:08.790
- [Mark] And you have all these emotions

00:11:08.790 --> 00:11:10.610
that must come up from this.

00:11:10.610 --> 00:11:12.690
- [J.J.] Yeah, I've never knew
how to deal with emotions.

00:11:12.690 --> 00:11:15.020
I messed up so many relationships

00:11:15.020 --> 00:11:16.503
because of the emotions.

00:11:17.960 --> 00:11:19.170
- [Mark] What do you deal with most?

00:11:19.170 --> 00:11:21.390
Is it anger, or depression, or anything?

00:11:21.390 --> 00:11:23.420
- [J.J.] Depression, I
believe it's depression

00:11:23.420 --> 00:11:25.930
and anxiety, is what I deal with most.

00:11:25.930 --> 00:11:28.890
And I've never been
treated for either one,

00:11:28.890 --> 00:11:30.440
so I don't know how to handle 'em,

00:11:30.440 --> 00:11:33.940
and sometimes I'd sleep for days.

00:11:33.940 --> 00:11:37.110
Like now, I just got up
after a two day sleep.

00:11:37.110 --> 00:11:38.730
It's like, I don't even
want to open my eyes

00:11:38.730 --> 00:11:42.610
and look at what I'm going
through in life, you know.

00:11:42.610 --> 00:11:44.800
So I just try to sleep it away,

00:11:44.800 --> 00:11:46.670
until I just have to get up, and go eat,

00:11:46.670 --> 00:11:48.363
and take care of myself.

00:11:50.610 --> 00:11:52.293
- [Mark] What was the
worst point in your life?

00:11:54.290 --> 00:11:56.633
- The worst part of my life was,

00:11:58.358 --> 00:12:00.273
I believe have to.

00:12:01.520 --> 00:12:03.173
I had a daughter,

00:12:04.480 --> 00:12:08.560
and because of all the
confusion in my head,

00:12:08.560 --> 00:12:10.570
I didn't know how to
even be a father to her.

00:12:10.570 --> 00:12:13.250
I didn't know how to say,
"Well, I went through this,

00:12:13.250 --> 00:12:15.567
so I'm gonna make sure
she had a better life."

00:12:16.460 --> 00:12:20.340
So my life just turned out

00:12:20.340 --> 00:12:22.240
where it was affecting
a young child's life,

00:12:22.240 --> 00:12:24.320
just like mines was affected,

00:12:24.320 --> 00:12:26.980
and where she had to go
stay with other people too.

00:12:26.980 --> 00:12:28.790
I just didn't know what
she had went through

00:12:28.790 --> 00:12:32.180
in her life, if it was similar to mine.

00:12:32.180 --> 00:12:36.880
So it was, I can say that was
the worst part of my life,

00:12:36.880 --> 00:12:40.617
having a child and not trying
to do better by that child,

00:12:40.617 --> 00:12:44.790
and not knowing if her life
was just as messed up as mine.

00:12:44.790 --> 00:12:47.193
- [Mark] What's your view on life?

00:12:48.470 --> 00:12:51.980
Is it just, people are evil,

00:12:51.980 --> 00:12:54.773
and it's a dog-eat-dog, and
just every man for himself?

00:12:56.393 --> 00:12:58.593
I mean, do you feel
betrayed by your family?

00:12:59.980 --> 00:13:02.520
- I think it's a little bit of all of it.

00:13:02.520 --> 00:13:05.620
I think if it would've
been more interest taken

00:13:05.620 --> 00:13:07.770
into me as a child,

00:13:07.770 --> 00:13:12.280
then maybe I would have
understood some things?

00:13:12.280 --> 00:13:13.113
- [Mark] It's easy for you to have

00:13:13.113 --> 00:13:16.060
a very negative view on existence.

00:13:16.060 --> 00:13:17.710
- Right, yes, exactly.

00:13:17.710 --> 00:13:18.543
- [Mark] With what you went through.

00:13:18.543 --> 00:13:21.800
- I would have been able to
see things more positive,

00:13:21.800 --> 00:13:24.240
and separate some of
the things and saying,

00:13:24.240 --> 00:13:27.770
okay, that happened, and it
was a bad thing that happened,

00:13:27.770 --> 00:13:29.660
but just told to move on,

00:13:29.660 --> 00:13:32.100
that I'm a good person, or something.

00:13:32.100 --> 00:13:34.363
I've never had that
positive input, really,

00:13:36.331 --> 00:13:37.164
a lot of times.

00:13:37.164 --> 00:13:40.590
So my view of life is that,

00:13:40.590 --> 00:13:44.460
it was just a bad place.

00:13:44.460 --> 00:13:45.773
People were all bad.

00:13:46.660 --> 00:13:49.860
Nobody really understood or
cared about the next person.

00:13:49.860 --> 00:13:52.360
It was all about what
they can get out of life.

00:13:52.360 --> 00:13:55.103
And I was just a pawn in it,

00:13:56.680 --> 00:13:59.550
and people were selfish.

00:13:59.550 --> 00:14:02.522
They didn't really care
about me or anybody else.

00:14:02.522 --> 00:14:04.000
- [Mark] What's the most important lesson

00:14:04.000 --> 00:14:05.970
you've learned in your life?

00:14:05.970 --> 00:14:08.260
- The most important
lesson I learned in life,

00:14:08.260 --> 00:14:09.403
is not to give up.

00:14:11.200 --> 00:14:13.210
Like I said, even though
I've been down here

00:14:13.210 --> 00:14:15.850
all these years, even though
I went through everything

00:14:15.850 --> 00:14:16.710
I went through in life,

00:14:16.710 --> 00:14:18.540
I think the most in
person lesson I learned,

00:14:18.540 --> 00:14:20.530
is not to give up on it.

00:14:20.530 --> 00:14:25.170
That it is my life, and it's
mine to make the best of.

00:14:25.170 --> 00:14:29.010
So each day I get up, I
stand and I still think

00:14:29.010 --> 00:14:30.670
that something's gonna happen for me.

00:14:30.670 --> 00:14:32.610
Something good is gonna happen,

00:14:32.610 --> 00:14:34.110
and all this would turn around.

00:14:34.110 --> 00:14:36.020
And I think I'll just
continue to think that,

00:14:36.020 --> 00:14:37.850
and believed that until the day I go.

00:14:37.850 --> 00:14:38.868
- [Mark] You still have hope.

00:14:38.868 --> 00:14:39.701
- I still have hope.

00:14:39.701 --> 00:14:41.057
- [Mark] That's excellent,
that's great to hear.

00:14:41.057 --> 00:14:42.440
- I have to hope that--

00:14:42.440 --> 00:14:43.330
- [Mark] You should.

00:14:43.330 --> 00:14:44.163
- Thank you.

00:14:45.230 --> 00:14:47.360
- [Mark] Do you ever have urges to do

00:14:47.360 --> 00:14:50.850
what was done to you with children?

00:14:50.850 --> 00:14:52.023
That's a common story.

00:14:53.270 --> 00:14:55.820
- Not to a child, not to a child.

00:14:55.820 --> 00:14:58.070
I think because it was
done to me as a child.

00:15:00.429 --> 00:15:04.780
I think it's the wrong
thing to do to a child.

00:15:04.780 --> 00:15:06.290
I think when I was younger,

00:15:06.290 --> 00:15:10.530
I didn't know the difference
between a child and adult.

00:15:10.530 --> 00:15:11.840
And so I didn't understand

00:15:11.840 --> 00:15:13.880
what was being done to me was wrong.

00:15:13.880 --> 00:15:16.990
But as I grew older, I
understood it was wrong,

00:15:16.990 --> 00:15:18.690
because I was a kid.

00:15:18.690 --> 00:15:23.530
So to a child, no, I
don't understand that,

00:15:23.530 --> 00:15:26.030
because I didn't understand
what was done to me,

00:15:26.030 --> 00:15:27.420
and I wouldn't want another child

00:15:27.420 --> 00:15:28.583
to have to go through that.

00:15:28.583 --> 00:15:29.683
- [Mark] Good for you.

00:15:32.230 --> 00:15:33.280
Yeah, you've been through a lot.

00:15:33.280 --> 00:15:36.250
That kinda derails the
way your brain works

00:15:36.250 --> 00:15:37.270
after that, doesn't it?

00:15:37.270 --> 00:15:38.103
- Yes, it does.

00:15:38.103 --> 00:15:39.467
I mean, I think I'm a failure,

00:15:39.467 --> 00:15:43.250
and still a fairly intelligent person.

00:15:43.250 --> 00:15:45.470
And like I said, I have tried
to reach and get out of here.

00:15:45.470 --> 00:15:47.950
I believe every situation
I've been put in,

00:15:47.950 --> 00:15:51.860
in life coming up, and
the people I've met,

00:15:51.860 --> 00:15:54.670
was something that

00:15:55.630 --> 00:15:59.270
I needed to learn to
continue to cope with life.

00:15:59.270 --> 00:16:02.130
The good and the bad
has all been just things

00:16:02.130 --> 00:16:05.210
to help me become a better person.

00:16:05.210 --> 00:16:09.120
And like I said, I still want the best.

00:16:09.120 --> 00:16:11.740
I still want to believe that someday

00:16:11.740 --> 00:16:13.770
this will all be behind me,

00:16:13.770 --> 00:16:17.530
and I can achieve something out of life,

00:16:17.530 --> 00:16:20.820
and maybe help others that
went through the same thing.

00:16:20.820 --> 00:16:21.653
I don't know.

00:16:21.653 --> 00:16:23.810
Maybe I can talk about it one day.

00:16:23.810 --> 00:16:26.170
There's other people
just like me out there

00:16:26.170 --> 00:16:28.670
who needs some type of a guidance.

00:16:28.670 --> 00:16:29.790
And I can tell them what it took

00:16:29.790 --> 00:16:32.380
for me to just live this long,

00:16:32.380 --> 00:16:36.590
and continue to believe that
life is gonna be okay for me.

00:16:36.590 --> 00:16:37.870
- [Mark] Yeah, you deserve everything

00:16:37.870 --> 00:16:38.750
that life has to offer.

00:16:38.750 --> 00:16:40.269
- Yes, exactly.

00:16:40.269 --> 00:16:41.950
- [Mark] I hope it comes your way.

00:16:41.950 --> 00:16:43.110
- Yes, exactly.

00:16:43.110 --> 00:16:44.080
- [Mark] All right,
J.J., thank you so much

00:16:44.080 --> 00:16:45.533
for sharing your story.

00:16:45.533 --> 00:16:46.366
- And thank you,

00:16:46.366 --> 00:16:47.199
- [Mark] I wish you the best of luck.

00:16:47.199 --> 00:16:48.163
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

00:16:51.217 --> 00:16:54.690
- You know, I haven't told
nobody that whole story before.

00:16:54.690 --> 00:16:55.523
- [Mark] Really?

00:16:55.523 --> 00:16:57.870
- Never told anybody that whole story

00:16:57.870 --> 00:16:59.013
- [Mark] How's it feel?

00:17:01.700 --> 00:17:04.190
- Well, it feels okay,

00:17:04.190 --> 00:17:06.963
and then I feel like, 'cause
what is my family gonna say?

00:17:06.963 --> 00:17:08.800
Because I've never told 'em

00:17:08.800 --> 00:17:11.110
- [Mark] Well, I mean, (chuckles)

00:17:11.110 --> 00:17:14.400
they really can't condemn
you for talking about.

00:17:14.400 --> 00:17:15.233
They're the ones that should be.

00:17:15.233 --> 00:17:16.690
- Well maybe they need to know.

00:17:16.690 --> 00:17:17.850
- [Mark] I would say so, yeah.

00:17:17.850 --> 00:17:19.500
- Maybe they need to
know, but I have never sat

00:17:19.500 --> 00:17:21.590
and told anyone that whole story before,

00:17:21.590 --> 00:17:24.270
and maybe all this happened

00:17:24.270 --> 00:17:27.960
because it's time that
somebody needs to know.

00:17:27.960 --> 00:17:30.600
Wow, that's why he's going through that.

00:17:30.600 --> 00:17:31.590
That's why he got.

00:17:31.590 --> 00:17:33.490
- [Mark] I mean, as an
outsider who just met you,

00:17:33.490 --> 00:17:34.323
looking at you,

00:17:34.323 --> 00:17:35.390
you're handsome, you're intelligent.

00:17:35.390 --> 00:17:36.360
You speak beautifully.

00:17:36.360 --> 00:17:39.340
You present yourself really well,

00:17:39.340 --> 00:17:40.970
and yet I'm sure you have
this very negative view

00:17:40.970 --> 00:17:43.200
of yourself, because of that childhood.

00:17:43.200 --> 00:17:44.033
- Yeah, I do.

00:17:44.033 --> 00:17:45.110
- [Mark] Not just the molestation,

00:17:45.110 --> 00:17:46.750
but everything else, the
way you were treated.

00:17:46.750 --> 00:17:47.583
- Yeah,

00:17:48.782 --> 00:17:50.800
- [Mark] And you deserve any of that.

00:17:50.800 --> 00:17:53.700
You deserve to live the best
life you can possibly dream of.

00:17:53.700 --> 00:17:55.160
- Yeah.

00:17:55.160 --> 00:17:56.100
- [Mark] And yet you're here on Skid Row

00:17:56.100 --> 00:17:57.670
living like a...

00:17:57.670 --> 00:17:58.940
- Yeah, I don't know what to say.

00:17:58.940 --> 00:17:59.773
- [Mark] And I'm like, it does.

00:17:59.773 --> 00:18:00.606
When you came walking up, I'm like,

00:18:00.606 --> 00:18:01.800
well he's not. (chuckles)

00:18:01.800 --> 00:18:02.633
- Yeah.

00:18:02.633 --> 00:18:04.250
- [Mark] He's not somebody
I want to interview,

00:18:04.250 --> 00:18:05.840
but your story is incredible.

00:18:05.840 --> 00:18:06.770
- Thank you.

00:18:06.770 --> 00:18:07.760
- [Mark] You don't deserve a bit of it.

00:18:07.760 --> 00:18:08.593
Thank you man.

00:18:08.593 --> 00:18:10.142
- [Mark] No one does.

00:18:10.142 --> 00:18:11.725
- I appreciate you.

